   "claim": "1,568 children, 319 fewer than the FY2003 peak \u2014 and the fall stopped in FY2015.",
   "detail": "The argument in town assumes enrolment is falling. It fell \u2014 17.5% from FY2003 to FY2015 \u2014 and then it stopped. The peak was FY2003 at 1,887. The low was FY2015 at 1,557. Every year since has been within 92 of that low, and FY2026 is 1,568. A budget built on a falling headcount is built on a decade-old trend.",
